{
  "title": "Osteochondritis Dissecans of Elbow",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/shoulder-and-elbow/3085/osteochondritis-dissecans-of-elbow",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Oct 19 2025",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Osteochondritis Dissecans of Elbow is a localized injury and subsequent separation of articular cartilage and subchondral bone of the capitellum, most commonly seen in gymnasts and pitchers.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis can be made with plane radiographs but MRI studies can be helpful to evaluate for the size of lesion and extent of bony edema.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment can be nonoperative or operative depending on size of the lesion, stability of the lesion, and presence of loose bodies.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "usually occurs after age 10 (typically adolescents)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "juvenille OCD better prognosis than adult",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "boys more common than girls",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Anatomic location",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "typically located in **capitellum of dominant upper extremity**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Risk factors",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "repetitive overhead and upper extremity weight bearing activities",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**gymnasts and throwing**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "theorized to result from repetitive compression-type injury (overhead or upper extremity weight bearing activities) of the immature capitellum causing",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "vascular insufficiency",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "repetitive microtrauma",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Associated conditions",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**Panner's disease (osteochondrosis of the capitellum)**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "typically presents in first decade of life (<10 years old)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "usually **benign** self-limiting course with no functional deficits",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "same mechanism of injury as OCD",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "surgery is contraindicated for Panner disease (unlike OCD elbow)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Anatomy",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Capitellum is supplied by 2 end arteries",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3085/images/screen_shot_2017-04-07_at_9.40.56_pm.jpg",
              "caption": "Blood supply"
            }
          ],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "radial recurrent artery",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "interosseous recurrent artery",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Classification",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "",
          "table": [
            {
